 <46025606+Ken5998@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 02:42:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(linux): export the vsync and guest_vblank_rate cvars from
 the gpu plugin

Saints Reborn reads and sets vsync and guest_vblank_rate, which live in
the GPU plugin. On Windows the plugin exports all its symbols; on Linux
it is built with hidden visibility, so the game did not link. Those two
are now exported with default visibility.
---
 include/rex/graphics/flags.h | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/rex/graphics/flags.h b/include/rex/graphics/flags.h
index 1e43481..b9fffb5 100644
--- a/include/rex/graphics/flags.h
+++ b/include/rex/graphics/flags.h
@@ -14,8 +14,15 @@
 #include <rex/cvar.h>
 
 // GPU Core
-REXCVAR_DECLARE(bool, vsync);
-REXCVAR_DECLARE(double, guest_vblank_rate);
+// The game reads and sets these two in the GPU plugin. On Windows the plugin
+// exports all its symbols; elsewhere only the ones marked for export.
+#if defined(_WIN32)
+#define REX_GPU_CVAR_EXPORT
+#else
+#define REX_GPU_CVAR_EXPORT __attribute__((visibility("default")))
+#endif
+REX_GPU_CVAR_EXPORT REXCVAR_DECLARE(bool, vsync);
+REX_GPU_CVAR_EXPORT REXCVAR_DECLARE(double, guest_vblank_rate);
 REXCVAR_DECLARE(bool, clear_memory_page_state);
 REXCVAR_DECLARE(bool, half_pixel_offset);
 REXCVAR_DECLARE(bool, async_shader_compilation);
